/*--------------------------------*- Choupo -*--------------------------------*\
  chemistry/H2P2O7-formation.dat -- the first 2 dissociations of pyrophosphoric acid, written from the master:
      H4P2O7  <=>  H2P2O7 + 2 H+

  logK25 and dH are the PRINTED values of the sources below (standard state ideal solution at 1 mol/kg, 298.15 K):
      pK1 = 0.83, dH1 = -9.2 kJ/mol, dCp ~-90 J/mol/K
      pK2 = 2.26, dH2 = -5.0 kJ/mol, dCp ~-130 J/mol/K
      pK3 = 6.72, dH3 = 0.5 kJ/mol, dCp -136 J/mol/K
      pK4 = 9.46, dH4 = 1.4 kJ/mol, dCp -141 J/mol/K
  Source: Goldberg, Kishore & Lennen, J. Phys. Chem. Ref. Data 31 (2002) 231; standard state: hypothetical ideal solution of unit molality, 298.15 K, 0.1 MPa (Section 8, p. 359).
  This record carries the sum of the first 2 steps (the sign flips with the direction written).
  The constant-dCp term of the printed dCp is NOT carried: the record grammar has no place for it (a
  van't Hoff integral with a constant dCp is exactly the `analytic` A1, A3, A4 terms; proposed, not done).
  The catalogue family is `phosphate`; pyrophosphate joins it for navigation.
\*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
recordType aqueousSpeciation;
schemaVersion 1;

species H2P2O7; masters ( { ion H4P2O7; nu 1; } { ion H; nu -2; } );
      logK25 -3.09; dH -14200; source "Goldberg, Kishore & Lennen, J. Phys. Chem. Ref. Data 31 (2002) 231 -- Section 8 summary, p. 360, and Section 7.56, p. 333: pK1 0.83, dH1 -9.2 kJ/mol, pK2 2.26, dH2 -5.0 kJ/mol (pK, dH_ion at 298.15 K)";
